CASE SOURCE — no steps exist in AWPTCM or ck.db (queue issue I-2)
================================================================================
No ck.db case was mapped onto this one; that would fabricate a source. Graded against:

1. Software TPS — wiki "X960_platform_support_TPS" (fetched from tb277, 70,440 B).
   Row 25, group "DHCP server": feature "DHCP 120-day lease", priority 1, supported = **Yes**.
   ⇒ UNSUPPORTED is not available without DUT evidence.
2. Wiki "DHCP" feature page, section "120 Lease", verbatim:
   "Simple enhancement feature which allows a user to configure lease times up to 120 days.
    The maximum used to be 30 days (set by IP Infusion)."
   ⇒ The feature IS the raised ceiling. The boundary is therefore the heart of the case, not
     an extra: 120 must be accepted and 121 must be refused.
3. AW+ CLI command page `lease.md`: `lease <days> <hours> <minutes> [<seconds>]`,
   "<days> The number of days, from 0 to 120 ... Default: 1", plus `lease infinite` / `no lease`.
   Mode: DHCP Configuration (the pool's `awplus(dhcp-config)#`).
4. DHCP Feature Overview and Configuration Guide (C613-22102-00 REV G) p13, "Set the lease".

120 days = 120 x 86400 = **10,368,000 s**, the value DHCP option 51 must carry.

