        Status:       Enabled      [Enabled]
        Type:         ARP          [Ping]                   <- T43851's settings survived
        Packets:      3            [5]
        Timeout:      1000 msecs   [200]
    DHCP Server service is enabled / DHCP Server is running

Proven on the wire after the reload, not only in the show — fresh client 02:c4:00:00:02:01:
      ARP probes seen = 3   gaps = [0.995 s, 1.001 s]   all for 192.168.10.105
      OFFER 192.168.10.105   opt51 = 10368000
      ACK   192.168.10.105   opt51 = 10368000
Both features still behave exactly as configured after a reboot. PERSISTENCE PASS for both cases.

INCIDENTAL, worth carrying forward: the DUT clock SURVIVED the reload
(`show clock` -> Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:38:52 +0000). So the year-2000 reading seen at probe time
was a stale RTC state, not a reset-on-every-boot trait of this model. A future campaign on this
unit does not need to re-repair the clock after each reboot — only once, if it has sat unpowered.

