3. Group bench teardown. The first attempt stopped partway — recorded because it is exactly the
   trap memory `bench-scripts-stop-on-cli-errors` describes, and cfg.py behaved correctly:
     awplus(config)# no interface vlan10
     % Removal of interface not allowed
   cfg.py exited 2 at that line and SKIPPED every command after it, leaving port1.0.10 still in
   VLAN 10. The `no interface vlan<N>` form is not supported on AW+; a VLAN interface is removed
   by deleting the VLAN from the vlan database. Had the driver hidden the "% " line or carried
   on, the bench would have been left half-restored and the post-run probe would have been the
   first thing to notice. Completed with:
     interface port1.0.10 / switchport access vlan 1
     vlan database / no vlan 10                                 (cfg.py exit 0, no "% " lines)

