================================================================================
VERDICT: PASS -- a 120-day lease is configurable and is delivered as DHCP option 51 =
10,368,000 s in both the OFFER and the ACK, with a binding expiry exactly 120 days out; the
parser accepts 120 and refuses 121 and 999, which is the 30->120 day enhancement itself; other
lease values (1 day, 1 hour) deliver their own option 51 in the same run; `no lease` restores
the 1-day default on the wire and clears the running-config; and the setting survives a reboot.
Options 58/59 are not emitted by this server and were recorded, not required.
